Root cause:
The bug was caused by incorrect handling of the bootloader family configuration, specifically the block size and device configuration access. The previous implementation assumed a default block size of 2048 bytes and did not properly check for the presence of a family configuration, leading to potential null pointer dereferences and incorrect behavior when accessing device configuration offsets. The patch corrects these issues by adjusting the block size to 1024 bytes for the bootloader and ensuring that checks for family configuration are appropriately implemented.
